/* ============================================================
   Logo Intro — startup/logo screen ("title"). The app's very first screen:
   the final logo_intro.mp4 animation, played once full-bleed against a
   near-black backdrop (TitleController advances to Lore when the video
   ends, or immediately on a tap/click anywhere). Palette custom properties
   (--base …) cascade in from .mikey-app in theme.uss; this file only adds
   Title-specific structure, same pattern as Home/Home.uss, Intro/Intro.uss.

   Deliberately minimal: no CTA, no subtitle, no static logo image — the
   video itself is the logo mark. .safe-area-content is still present (every
   screen has exactly one, see MikeyAppUxmlTests) but stays empty: a
   full-bleed cinematic has no foreground content that needs to dodge device
   safe-area insets.

   Title intentionally uses pure #000000 here instead of the shared --base
   near-black: on wider landscape screens scale-to-fit letterboxes the 16:9
   video, and --base's faint blue-gray tint reads as a visible bar next to
   the video's own black. Pure black blends the letterbox seamlessly into
   the animation instead.
   ============================================================ */

.title-screen {
    padding: 0;
    background-color: #000000;
}

/* ---------- full-bleed backdrop + logo video ----------
   Lives OUTSIDE .safe-area-content so it bleeds under device insets, like
   .intro-bg / .home-bg / .combine-bg on the other screens. .title-bg's solid
   black is both the "black background immediately" backdrop shown before
   playback starts and the letterbox color around the video once it plays.
   .title-video sits on top of it with scale-to-fit, so the animation fills
   the screen without ever stretching, distorting or being cropped. */
.title-bg {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    background-color: #000000;
}

.title-video {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}

/* ---------- final-logo hold ----------
   The static Mikey logo image, framed with the same full-bleed scale-to-fit
   sizing as .title-video so crossfading between them (TitleController's
   AdvanceRoutine) reads as seamless rather than a jump cut. Hidden by
   default (opacity 0) — only shown once advancing has begun, so the video
   itself is what plays under normal viewing. */
.title-logo-hold {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    background-image: url("/Assets/UI/Media/Images/mikey_logo.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
    opacity: 0;
}
